      "mother": {
        "preparation": {
          "model_calls": 1,
          "phase": "preparation",
          "plan": {
            "A": "Research low-risk copy and allocation elimination. Pass read-only graph, matrix, edge-list and lookup-vector arguments by const reference, especially in deep, coresConjunto, Prim_ST, is_cycle and find_min_key. Initially retain history-by-value so traversal behavior stays unchanged. Replace create_partitions' full scan for the last partition with back/pop_back; move partition payloads only where ownership genuinely transfers. Reserve predictable capacities and avoid redundant local copies without invalidating references. Preserve partition insertion order and all comparisons. Measure copy-only and container changes separately.",
            "B": "Research the spanning-tree path evaluator: buscaAresta, deep, coresConjunto and caminhoTropi. Build adjacency once per spanning tree by scanning its edge vector in order and appending both directions, exactly reproducing buscaAresta's neighbor order. Use one backtracked path, visited flags and color-frequency counters with an incremental distinct-color count. Compress observed color IDs if useful, but retain the original nCores target. Preserve ascending starting vertices, leaf-only success checks, first-success behavior, strict-greater fallback updates, isolated-start behavior and output formatting. Do not stop at an internal prefix merely because it already contains every color. Avoid rescanning edges or recounting path colors at each recursive call.",
            "C": "Research deterministic constrained-Prim acceleration. Establish that committed parent edges form a forest and every candidate joins a selected vertex to an unselected vertex; then remove the redundant cycle checker and mat_cycle allocation. Replace new_mat copies with immutable adjacency plus symmetric exclusion marks. Preserve root 0, lowest-index key ties, ascending neighbor processing, strict key comparisons, included-edge processing order, literal sentinel rules and the distinction between discovered and selected vertices. Compare a streamlined dense implementation with sorted adjacency and a minimum-vertex frontier: all usable edges have unit weight, so discovery occurs once. Preserve parent-pair emission order, failure behavior and partition generation order. Do not substitute an arbitrary spanning-tree algorithm or reinterpret the inclusion rules.",
            "G": "Integrate only candidates validated by the unchanged correctness harness. Preserve the exact selected path, color count and formatting, not merely an equally good path. Measure each standalone winner and staged combinations; A overlaps B and C, so gains are not additive. Retain the fastest measured passing program even when that is an uncombined child. Given the baseline sample spread, require repeatable timing evidence for small gains and avoid default threading at this runtime scale. Keep tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target and permissions unchanged; allow no expected-answer substitution or input-specific specialization.",
            "analysis": "The relevant task is Problem A, src/tropical.cpp. This run's baseline passes four cases and averages 7.928 ms, with samples spanning 7.638–8.343 ms. No input sizes or hotspot measurements are supplied. Source inspection suggests expensive repeated graph/vector copies, cycle-check matrix copies, per-node tree-edge scans, leaf color recounting and partition-stack scans. On the four-core ARM64 target without GPUs, prioritize deterministic serial overhead reductions before parallel startup costs. Output depends on spanning-tree, partition and DFS order: the reference returns the first tropical leaf, or the first strictly improving maximum-color fallback. The research therefore preserves those choices rather than replacing the search with a different optimal-path algorithm. All transformations must remain general and correct for every valid input."
          },
