              "C": "Research exact case-generation acceleration independently of sorting. Preserve the two MWC recurrences, seed reset, unsigned combination, abs/conversion behavior, floating-point drand expression and resulting native integer bytes. Do not assume multiplication followed by division and integer truncation can simply be removed. Investigate independent generation blocks using mathematically derived MWC jump-ahead: each recurrence is multiplication by a modulo a*65536-1 for its applicable states, with exceptional states handled explicitly. Start each block at its exact preceding state, generate every element, and restore the exact final global states if the original quicksort remains reachable. Compare interleaved independent lanes with supported parallel blocks, including jump-ahead overhead. Require a correctness argument for the entire sequence, not merely matching sampled checksums.",
              "G": "Keep the validated baseline and best standalone candidate available. Treat A and B as alternative sorting backends; integrate the winner with C in separately measured variants rather than assuming cumulative gains. Consider generation/histogram fusion or shared worker infrastructure only after simpler combinations are correct and faster; preserve the distinction between permutation-invariant global histograms and pass-dependent chunk histograms. Use the unchanged harness and budgets, comparing complete-process timings because the baseline is only about 70 ms. Preserve stdin handling, error behavior, validation, checksum macro behavior, native-byte MD5 order and allocation fallbacks. Reason through small sizes, duplicates, signed values, uneven chunks and ownership boundaries. Never replace generation or hashing with cached results, specialize to tested sizes, change the environment, or select a slower integration merely because its components improved separately.",
