            "analysis": "The relevant program is Sokoban's unit-player-move BFS over the player position and sorted box positions. Plausible costs are repeated box scans, copying/sorting/hashing successors, chained visited lookups, and pointer-heavy state storage; no profile establishes their relative importance. This run's baseline passed four correctness cases and averaged 4.982 ms across three samples, ranging from 4.816 to 5.116 ms. Consequently, favor low-overhead sequential experiments on the four-core ARM64 target rather than assuming threading will help. Preserve shortest total player movement, exact state identity, and deterministic first-parent behavior. In particular, the source generates right, left, up, down but prepends each next-layer frontier; switching to conventional FIFO up/down/left/right traversal can change the oracle-visible path. All proposed changes must remain general across valid inputs, not encode measured boards or expected solutions."
